  "content": {
    "id": "p6-p4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "For $a\\ne b$, show that the line passing through $(a,b)$ and $(b,a)$ is $y=a+b-x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m=-1$, so $y-b=-(x-a)$ and hence $y=a+b-x$.",
      "worked": "Since $a\\ne b$,\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=\\frac{a-b}{b-a}\\\\m&=-1\\\\y-b&=-1(x-a)\\\\y-b&=-x+a\\\\y&=a+b-x\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
